        "content": "<p>A monoid congruence <code>~</code> is an equivalence relation on a (multiplicative) monoid <code>M</code> that is compatible with <code>1</code> and <code>*</code>.  Then we can form the quotient monoid <code>M / ~</code> and get a surjective monoid homomorphism <code>f : M → M / ~</code>.  Where are these results in Mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 620838533,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1788309863
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Con#doc\">docs#Con</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Con.Quotient#doc\">docs#Con.Quotient</a></p>",
